# The repo is a complete working copy on purpose: backend/.env and its real
# API keys are tracked, so a clone runs without re-collecting credentials.
# That is only safe while this repository stays private — making it public, or
# adding a collaborator, hands out every key in it, and git history keeps them
# even after a later deletion. Rotate the keys if either happens.

# Build artifacts of the two package managers. Not source: 1.4 GB of
# machine-local virtualenv with absolute paths baked in, and 94 MB of
# node_modules. requirements.txt and package-lock.json reproduce both exactly.
.venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
dist/

# The Google Lens result cache (app/lens_cache.py). Regenerable by re-running
# the search, 30-day TTL, and every entry costs SerpApi quota to refill — worth
# keeping on disk between runs, not worth committing.
backend/.cache/

# CLIP's ViT-B-32.pt is 338 MB — past GitHub's hard 100 MB per-file limit, so
# it cannot be pushed without Git LFS. Downloaded on first run.
backend/weights/

# The Winning Products snapshot archive (app/snapshot_store.py). Machine-local
# and append-only: it grows with every scan and each machine's copy diverges
# immediately, so committing it would mean a binary merge conflict per run.
# backend/fixtures/ carries the captured scan that seeds it — re-seed with
# `python -m scripts.scan_winning`.
backend/data/
